cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AcousticBench, please cite the software and the underlying dataset."
title: "AcousticBench — Electroacoustic Measurement, Validation & Reporting Toolkit"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible toolkit for electroacoustic measurement analysis,
  signal-processing validation and automated engineering reports. It provides
  MATLAB and Python implementations of core measurement algorithms, a
  Streamlit research dashboard, a virtual hearing aid, a 1000-case synthetic
  validation suite and sixteen reproducible experiments.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-16"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/example/AcousticBench"
keywords:
  - electroacoustics
  - hearing aids
  - real-ear measurement
  - probe tube
  - digital signal processing
  - measurement automation
  - reproducible research
authors:
  - name: "AcousticBench contributors"
